   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "14d9af19",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Data representation and distance (what we are measuring)\n",
    "\n",
    "The clustering input is the output of a preprocessing pipeline that:\n",
    "- **Numerical features** (`adults`, `children`, `babies`, `stays_in_weekend_nights`, `stays_in_week_nights`, `lead_time`) are **median-imputed** (for missing `children`) and **standardized** to make Euclidean distance meaningful.\n",
    "- **Categorical features** (`hotel`, `arrival_date_month`, `market_segment`) are **mode-imputed** (if missing) and **one-hot encoded** with `handle_unknown=\"ignore\"` to ensure safe transformation at inference.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Feature Exclusions (Leakage Control & Profiling‑only Variables)**\n",
    "- **meal**: Often reflects product/package selection (HB/BB/SC) or property offerings rather than guest behaviour; it can act as a marketing/product confounder. Excluded from the clustering input; used for cluster profiling/interpretation only.\n",
    "- **customer_type**: Encodes administrative booking segments (e.g., Contract, Group, Transient) that can dominate behavioural signals. Kept for post‑hoc profiling, not as an input to derive behaviour‑driven clusters.\n",
    "- **deposit_type**: Payment policy (no/partial/non‑refundable) is an operational/contractual attribute that may correlate with promotions or property rules; treated as profiling‑only to avoid clustering on payment policy rather than guest behaviour.\n",
    "- **reserved_room_type**: Room allocation at booking can reflect availability or later operational changes and therefore leak property decisions. Excluded from the representation.\n",
    "- **country**: High cardinality and demographic in nature; it can overwhelm behavioural signals and raises privacy concerns. Excluded from the numeric/categorical representation.\n",
    "- **previous_history** (prior cancellations/bookings): Historical outcome/activity fields behave like label‑like information and can bias segmentation toward past outcomes. Used for profiling/validation, not as clustering inputs.\n",
    "- **parking** (parking spaces / parking_required): Operational/resource attribute that varies by property and is a weak behavioural signal; excluded from inputs and to be used only for cluster summaries if useful.\n",
    "- **special_requests**: Free‑text or sparse semi‑structured requests are noisy and may contain operational/sensitive details.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Final feature space:** standardized numeric dimensions + binary hotel indicator + one-hot booking context variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Similarity/distance metric implied by the representation:**  \n",
    "Euclidean distance in the transformed space, combining standardized continuous values with one-hot categorical vectors. This is the distance minimized by KMeans.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hotel control comparison:**  \n",
    "We compare two variants:\n",
    "- `with_hotel`: includes the hotel indicator;\n",
    "- `without_hotel`: excludes hotel so clustering is driven by booking behavior and booking-time context alone.\n",
    "\n",
    "This comparison tests whether `hotel` is a useful segmentation signal or a dataset-level confounder.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Feature exclusions (leakage control):**\n",
    "- Post-booking outcome fields such as `is_canceled`, `reservation_status`, `reservation_status_date` are **excluded** and never used for clustering.\n",
    "- Any variable that could reflect post-booking operational decisions (e.g. `assigned_room_type`, `booking_changes`) is excluded at this stage."
   ]
  },
