    "* **Short-stay vs. Extended-stay Segments**: The numerical heatmap distinctly separates groups by `stays_in_week_nights` and `stays_in_weekend_nights`, clearly identifying extended stay leisure guests vs. brief transient guests.\n",
    "* **Family vs. Individual/Couple Behavior**: The `adults`, `children`, and `babies` indicators successfully isolated distinct \"Family\" clusters (spikes in children/babies) from solo travelers and couples.\n",
    "* **Market Segment Context**: The stacked bar charts reveal that certain behavioral clusters are heavily dominated by specific market segments (e.g., Online TA vs Groups), validating that the clusters capture real-world booking channels without post-booking data leakage.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Final Conclusion:** We successfully answered RQ1. Distinct, natural segments of guests emerge natively from pre-arrival booking data. The `without_hotel` variant proved that these behavioral profiles are universal across properties rather than artifacts of a specific hotel type. Furthermore, our stability testing demonstrated that the `KMeans` baseline is highly robust to initialization variations compared to hierarchical alternatives."
